# The Windows runner checks out with `core.autocrlf=true` system-wide, which
# rewrites every text file to CRLF. Goldens, generated `.d.ts` files and fixture
# round-trips compare bytes, so a CRLF checkout fails tests that have nothing to
# do with Windows. One line, LF everywhere, on every host.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Deliberately not text: the graph and the PNG goldens are bytes.
*.png -text
*.snap text eol=lf
*.d.ts text eol=lf
*.ets text eol=lf
